        11/3/71                                                SYS EXIT (II)


NAME              exit -- terminate process

SYNOPSIS          sys        exit    / exit = I

DESCRIPTION       exit is the normal means of terminating a process. All
                  files are closed and the parent process is notified if it
                  is executing a wait.

                  This call can never return.
FILES

SEE ALSO          sys wait

